Hi <%= @caregiver.display_name %>,

<% if @phone_failure == :could_not_place -%>
Remindly tried to call <%= @senior.display_name %> about <%= @reminder.title %> and could not get through.
<% if @scheduled_at -%>
It was due <%= @scheduled_at.strftime('%A, %B %d at %I:%M %p') %>. <%= pluralize(@attempts, "attempt") %> made,
and not one of them reached the phone network. That is a fault at our end.
<% end -%>
<% elsif @phone_failure == :not_attempted_in_time -%>
Remindly did not call <%= @senior.display_name %> about <%= @reminder.title %>.
<% if @scheduled_at -%>
It was due <%= @scheduled_at.strftime('%A, %B %d at %I:%M %p') %>, and was closed as missed
before Remindly managed to place the call. That is a fault at our end.
<% end -%>
<% elsif @phone_failure == :added_after_its_time -%>
Remindly did not call <%= @senior.display_name %> about <%= @reminder.title %>.
<% if @scheduled_at -%>
It was due <%= @scheduled_at.strftime('%A, %B %d at %I:%M %p') %>, but it was added to the
schedule after that time had already passed — usually because the reminder was added or
edited today. Remindly does not call about a time that has gone by, so no call was
placed for this one.
<% end -%>
<%# The same caveat the other no-call branches carry. In the HTML mail it sits
    outside the branches and covers every phone failure; here each branch has to
    say it, and a reader of the text-only mail would otherwise be left without
    the one sentence that separates "not asked" from "not done". -%>
Nobody was contacted, so this says nothing about whether <%= @senior.display_name %> did it —
only that Remindly did not ask.
<% elsif @phone_failure -%>
Remindly did not call <%= @senior.display_name %> about <%= @reminder.title %>.
<% if @scheduled_at -%>
It was due <%= @scheduled_at.strftime('%A, %B %d at %I:%M %p') %>, which is outside the hours
Remindly is allowed to place reminder calls — between <%= @calling_hours %> in
<%= @senior.display_name %>'s own time.
<% end -%>
Nobody was contacted, so this says nothing about whether <%= @senior.display_name %> did it —
only that Remindly did not ask.
<% else -%>
<%= @senior.display_name %> has not marked <%= @reminder.title %> as done.
<% if @scheduled_at -%>
It was due <%= @scheduled_at.strftime('%A, %B %d at %I:%M %p') %> and has not been marked done since.
<% end -%>
This means nobody pressed Done on their device. It does not necessarily mean it
was not done — they may have done it without marking it.
<% end -%>

View <%= @senior.display_name %>'s dashboard: <%= @dashboard_url %>

--
Remindly - Caregiver Coordination
You're receiving this because you're a caregiver for <%= @senior.display_name %>. You can turn these off in your notification settings.
